nd drone attacks. Iran rejected a US peace proposal. The conflict has caused over 3,000 deaths across the region. Diplomatic efforts continue despite ongoing hostilities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/middle-east-crisis-mediators-gather-in-pakistan-for-talks-on-ending-month-long-iran-war/articleshow/129881093.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/middle-east-crisis-mediators-gather-in-pakistan-for-talks-on-ending-month-long-iran-war/articleshow/129881093.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-03-29T19:02:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129881422,imgsize-82752.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘The Monkey Whisperer’: Florida man arrested for illegal trading of exotic animals]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129880457.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-monkey-whisperer-florida-man-arrested-for-illegal-trading-of-exotic-animals-fined-60000/articleshow/129880457.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-monkey-whisperer-florida-man-arrested-for-illegal-trading-of-exotic-animals-fined-60000/articleshow/129880457.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-03-29T17:54:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129880457,imgsize-137400.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Women need to shut up!’: Christian nationalist duo spark massive outrage with shocking viral rant]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129880186.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/women-need-to-shut-up-christian-nationalist-duo-spark-massive-outrage-with-shocking-viral-rant/articleshow/129880186.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/women-need-to-shut-up-christian-nationalist-duo-spark-massive-outrage-with-shocking-viral-rant/articleshow/129880186.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-03-29T17:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129880186,imgsize-95566.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Clavicular storms out of Andrew Callaghan interview after tense exchange over “looksmaxxing”]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129876351.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Clavicular abruptly ended an interview with Andrew Callaghan after the journalist said he was “satisfied” with his appearance. The comment clashed with Clavicular’s looksmaxxing ideology, leading to visible frustration and his exit. The viral clip highlights a deeper disconnect over self-image, expectations, and how online beliefs collide with real conversations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/clavicular-storms-out-of-andrew-callaghan-interview-after-tense-exchange-over-looksmaxxing/articleshow/129876351.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/clavicular-storms-out-of-andrew-callaghan-interview-after-tense-exchange-over-looksmaxxing/articleshow/129876351.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-03-29T17:06:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Barsha Dutta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129876351,imgsize-26410.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Owens Questions Missing Video: Candace Owens challenges Turning Point over Charlie clip; absence fuels doubt]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129874483.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Candace Owens has sparked debate by questioning why a video linked to an alleged audio of Charlie Kirk naming Erika Kirk as his successor has not been released. Her remarks have fueled online speculation, with many demanding transparency. While no verified video has surfaced, the absence of visual proof continues to raise doubts and keep the controversy alive.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/release-the-video-candace-owens-questions-missing-video-of-charlie-kirks-alleged-remarks-about-erika-kirk/articleshow/129874483.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/release-the-video-candace-owens-questions-missing-video-of-charlie-kirks-alleged-remarks-about-erika-kirk/articleshow/129874483.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-03-29T16:32:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Barsha Dutta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129874483,imgsize-42022.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Costcos are 90% Indian’: MAGA attacks Indian shoppers at stores with viral videos and 'invasion' claims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129878255.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/costcos-are-90-indian-maga-attacks-indian-shoppers-at-stores-with-videos-and-invasion-claims/articleshow/129878255.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/costcos-are-90-indian-maga-attacks-indian-shoppers-at-stores-with-videos-and-invasion-claims/articleshow/129878255.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-03-29T15:36:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129878255,imgsize-141376.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Al-Baha goes dark: Saudi city observes 'green hour' to cut carbon emissions]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129879170.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Al-Baha Municipality in Saudi Arabia participated in the "Al-Baha Green Hour" initiative, switching off non-essential lights for an hour to promote energy conservation and environmental protection. This local effort aligns with the broader Saudi Green Initiative, aiming to reduce carbon emissions and encourage responsible energy use among residents and in public spaces.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/al-baha-goes-dark-saudi-city-observes-green-hour-to-cut-carbon-emissions/articleshow/129879170.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/al-baha-goes-dark-saudi-city-observes-green-hour-to-cut-carbon-emissions/articleshow/129879170.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-03-29T16:29:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129879396,imgsize-328233.cms"/></item></channel></rss>